# The roster of people whose commits may land.
#
# CONTRIBUTING.md: each commit's author is the person who signs it off, a `Signed-off-by:` may only
# name someone who can make that certification, and a co-author trailer names a human contributor.
# The `authorship` check (.github/workflows/authorship.yml) enforces that against this file on
# every pull request. The DCO app and cla-assistant can't: they match a trailer against an author
# field and record an OAuth flow, and neither can ask whether a person stands behind the account.
#
# The check reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so a pull request can't admit its
# own author. Adding a line is a maintainer commit.
#
# Format: one person per line. The first token is the name we file them under; every token is an
# identity that person commits as. A token containing `@` is a git email (what a trailer is matched
# on), anything else is a GitHub login (what an author or committer is matched on).
#
#   <login>  <email>  [<more emails>]   # when, and anything worth knowing

bbz           429635+bbz@users.noreply.github.com              # maintainer

# GitHub itself, as the committer of a merge or squash made through the web UI.
web-flow      noreply@github.com                                # github.com merge button
